        <!-- SECTION 4: Coverage Chart -->
        <div id="coverage-chart" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Coverage Chart: Sq Ft Per Bag by Joint Size
          </h2>
          <p>
            If you'd rather do the math by hand, or want to sanity-check the calculator above, here's approximately how far a single 50-lb bag of polymeric jointing sand goes at common joint widths, assuming a standard 1.5-inch joint depth.
          </p>
          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <table class="w-full text-left">
              <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Joint Width</th>
                  <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Approx. Coverage per 50-lb Bag</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">1/8"</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">~90 sq ft</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                  <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">1/4"</td>
